        {
          "name": "engraving_check",
          "canonical_hash": "sha256:99da928ed4a69739e138d29ca5f7459a30710feebd2a0c61c11e8335e3ba0cae",
          "description": "Check a MusicXML score against The Gradus Engraving Rulebook. Runs 30+ statically-checkable rules (bar arithmetic, beaming vs meter, ties, voice separation, ledger/clef choice, expression marks) and returns findings located by part and measure, each carrying the published rule it violates — code, URL, and a ready-to-quote citation.\\n\\nWHY THIS EXISTS: LLM-generated notation is reliably badly engraved — bars that do not sum, ties between different pitches, beams across barlines — and there is no other public checker for engraving convention. Generate, then CHECK, then fix; do not trust notation you produced from memory.\\n\\nWHEN TO USE: after generating or editing MusicXML, before showing it to a user; when a user asks",
