          "name": "figured_bass_exercise",
          "canonical_hash": "sha256:6292e5acc74fafbc47d826f5179fb9637d8499c4fc34bbc6d103b378555a9d70",
          "description": "Fetch one figured-bass exercise by its permanent id, with the model realization, the citation line pre-formatted, its voice-leading cross-links resolved to named patterns, and the neighbouring exercises listed.\\n\\nWHEN TO USE: you already have an exercise id (from figured_bass_exercises, a Gradus URL, or a previous answer) and want the full entry — the given bass, the model realization, the teaching note on why it moves as it does, and keyboard guidance; you are walking a student forward or back through a stage via the neighbours.\\n\\nWHEN NOT TO USE: you do not know the id — search with figured_bass_exercises first. Guessing is fine though: a miss returns near-matching ids rather than a bare error, so you can correct in one more call.\\n\\nINPUT: { id: string } — the permanent exercise id, e.g.",
